---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Competitor Analysis for B2B SaaS"
  description="Source-verified competitor analysis for B2B SaaS teams covering product, pricing, positioning, recent moves and decision implications."
  path="/competitor-analysis/"
>
  <main class="ca">
    <section class="ca__hero" data-surface="dark"><div class="container-wide ca__grid"><div><span class="label">COMPETITOR ANALYSIS</span><h1>Compare competitors without pretending every public claim is equally reliable.</h1><p>Evidence Axis examines the competitor set, opens the underlying sources and compares the dimensions that matter to a real business decision. Facts, analytical readings and unresolved gaps remain visibly separate.</p><div class="ca__actions"><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=complimentary-brief">Request My Complimentary Brief <span>→</span></a><a href="/sample-report/">Inspect the sample analysis →</a></div></div><aside><small class="mono">TYPICAL DIMENSIONS</small><b>Product · Pricing · Positioning · Recent moves</b><p>The dimensions change when the decision requires something else. We do not force every project into the same comparison table.</p></aside></div></section>

    <section class="section ca__section"><div class="container-wide ca__grid"><div><span class="label">THE ANALYSIS</span><h2>Start with the question, then choose the comparison.</h2><p>A useful competitor analysis is narrower than a market encyclopedia. We define the decision boundary first, identify the competitors that belong in it, then collect and verify the evidence needed to compare them.</p></div><div class="ca__steps"><article><b>01</b><h3>Define the decision</h3><p>Pricing pressure, feature race, positioning conflict, sales objection, category move or another bounded question.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Validate the competitor set</h3><p>Known competitors are context, not automatically the complete set. Scan-derived candidates require evidence before promotion.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Verify the claims</h3><p>Open product pages, pricing, documentation, changelogs, filings or other relevant lawful public sources.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h3>Compare what matters</h3><p>Build the comparison around the decision rather than filling a generic matrix for appearance.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="section ca__section ca__section--paper"><div class="container-wide"><span class="label">EXAMPLE</span><h2>Intercom vs Zendesk, read as evidence.</h2><p class="ca__wide">The public Evidence Axis sample compares how Intercom and Zendesk position, package and substantiate their customer-support offerings. It also shows where public evidence cannot establish a universal winner or a workload-specific cost answer.</p><a class="btn" href="/sample-report/">Read the public sample <span>→</span></a></div></section>

    <section class="section ca__faq"><div class="container-wide"><span class="label">FAQ</span><h2>Questions teams usually ask before the work starts.</h2><details><summary>Can you analyze competitors we already know?</summary><p>Yes. Known competitors can be included, but Evidence Axis can also scan for overlooked candidates when the scope calls for discovery.</p></details><details><summary>Do you use vendor comparison pages?</summary><p>They can create useful leads, but vendor-authored comparison content is not treated as neutral proof for material claims.</p></details><details><summary>Can public evidence prove which competitor is best?</summary><p>Sometimes a bounded dimension can be established. A universal winner usually cannot. When the evidence does not support the conclusion, the result remains Unknown rather than being filled with an estimate.</p></details><details><summary>Can the analysis continue into sales or positioning work?</summary><p>Yes. A Competitive Response Sprint can turn a verified decision into battlecards, objection handling, pricing response, positioning or messaging assets.</p></details></div></section>

    <section class="section ca__cta" data-surface="dark"><div class="container ca__cta-inner"><span class="label">START WITH YOUR COMPANY</span><h2>See how the method reads against your competitive set.</h2><p>A verified company employee can request a complimentary company-specific brief without supplying a competitor list or booking a sales call first.</p><a class="btn btn--lg" href="/contact/?intent=complimentary-brief">Request My Complimentary Brief <span>→</span></a></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>
<style>
.ca{background:#fff}.ca__hero{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff;padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5.6rem) 0}.ca__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.08fr .92fr;gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem);align-items:start}.ca__hero h1,.ca h2{margin:.55rem 0 .9rem;font-size:clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5rem);line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.05em}.ca__hero p,.ca__section p,.ca__faq p,.ca__cta p{line-height:1.65}.ca__hero p{color:#b9c7d8;max-width:54rem}.ca__hero aside{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid rgba(120,160,210,.2);border-radius:.8rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.03)}.ca__hero aside small{display:block;color:#efb269;margin-bottom:.55rem}.ca__hero aside b{font-size:1.2rem}.ca__hero aside p{font-size:.88rem;margin:.7rem 0 0}.ca__actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.9rem;align-items:center;margin-top:1.3rem}.ca__actions>a:not(.btn){color:#efb269;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;text-decoration:none}.ca__section p,.ca__faq p{color:var(--text-muted)}.ca__steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.75rem}.ca__steps article{padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.12);border-radius:.75rem;background:#fff}.ca__steps b{font:800 .58rem/1 var(--font-mono);color:#a7642b}.ca__steps h3{margin:.5rem 0 .3rem}.ca__steps p{margin:0;font-size:.86rem}.ca__section--paper{background:#f3eee6}.ca__wide{max-width:65rem}.ca__faq details{border-top:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.15);padding:1rem 0}.ca__faq details:last-of-type{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(31,58,87,.15)}.ca__faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:1.05rem}.ca__faq details p{max-width:66rem;margin:.7rem 0 0}.ca__cta{background:#030914;color:#f4f8ff}.ca__cta-inner{text-align:center;max-width:66rem}.ca__cta-inner p{color:#a8b8cb;max-width:50rem;margin:.8rem auto 1.2rem}@media(max-width:860px){.ca__grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:560px){.ca__steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}.ca__actions{display:grid}.ca__actions a{width:100%}}
</style>
